      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Knee complaints may be the first symptom of retroperitoneal space-occupying processes, as a result of compression of the femoral or obturator nerve. This differential diagnostic possibility is pointed out with reference to four case histories. The importance of CT examination as a part of the diagnostic procedure is emphasised."},
